{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the people did not journey.</b> Because the cloud did not ascend. And great honor was done for her, that the cloud and all Israel waited for her seven days until she was healed. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted in tractate Sotah: with the measure a person measures, it is measured for him. Shimshon went after his eyes, as is said (Judges 14:3): ״אותה קח לי כי היא ישרה בעיני״ — and what is written of him? (ibid. 16) ״וינקרו פלשתים את עיניו״. Avshalom was prideful in his hair, therefore he was caught by his hair; and because he lay with ten of his father's concubines, ten spears were thrust into him, as is said (II Samuel 18:15): ״ויסבו עשרה נערים נושאי כלי יואב ויכו את אבשלום וימות״; and because he stole three hearts — the heart of his father, and the heart of the court, and the heart of all Israel — therefore three shafts were thrust into him, as is said (ibid.): ״ויקח שלשה שבטים בכפו ויתקעם בלב אבשלום עודנו חי בלב האלה״. And likewise regarding good: Yosef earned the right to his father's bones — there was none greater than him among his brothers, as is said (Genesis 50:7): ״ויעל יוסף לקבר את אביו״. Who is greater for us than Yosef, with whom none but Moshe occupied himself? Moshe earned the right to Yosef's bones — there was none greater than him in Israel, as is said (Exodus 13:19): ״ויקח משה את עצמות יוסף עמו״. Who is greater for us than Moshe, with whom none but the Shekhinah occupied itself, as is said (Deuteronomy 34:6): ״ויקברו אותו בגי״. And so we find regarding Miriam, that measure for measure was measured to her: she waited for Moshe one hour when he was cast into the Nile, as is said (Exodus 2:4): ״ותתצב אחותו מרחוק״; therefore all Israel was delayed on her account and waited for her seven days, as is said: ״והעם לא נסע עד האסף מרים״. End quote. And this is a well-known matter in several places, that the measure of the Holy One, blessed be He, is thus. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: even though four death penalties of the court were nullified, the judgment of four death penalties was not nullified. And this is a proof of particular providence in reward and punishment. And this is among the paths of righteousness and justice, as it says: ״כי אלהי משפט ה' אשרי כל חוכי לו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The closing quotation is from Isaiah 30:18 (the word חוכי is a ketiv/qere variant reading for חכי, 'those who wait for Him'); R. Bahya cites it without address, here left unattributed as in the source. The phrase 'with measure for measure' — מדה כנגד מדה — introduces the Sotah 11a teaching that he draws from the Talmudic passage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:05.335070402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}